<BaseLayout title="About & Editorial Policy" description="How Dama Korea researches, writes, updates and corrects its practical Korea guides."><section class="page-hero"><div class="shell"><span class="eyebrow">About Dama Korea</span><h1>Advice is useful only when you can see its limits.</h1><p>Dama Korea is an independent English-language guide for international visitors and new residents.</p></div></section><article class="article-shell article-body legal-page">
  <h2>Who runs Dama Korea</h2><p>Dama Korea is an independent publishing project based in South Korea, not a government body, travel agency or paid expert directory. It is operated under the Dama Korea publishing name. We do not invent a traveler, expert biography or first-person experience to make an article sound more authoritative.</p><p>We focus on the gap between a rule on an official page and the practical decision a reader still needs to make before or after arriving in Korea.</p>
  <h2>How we research</h2><p>Each guide starts with the responsible agency, transport operator, regulator or service provider. The editor turns those rules into a decision sequence, identifies failure points and checks whether a reader can complete the task without relying on an unstated assumption.</p><p>Official-source research, observation, interviews and first-hand experience are labeled rather than blended together. A source link does not mean that organization endorses Dama Korea.</p>
  <h2>Our publication checklist</h2><ul class="checklist"><li>The article answers one defined practical problem.</li><li>Time-sensitive claims link to the responsible source.</li><li>Limitations and cases that vary are visible near the advice.</li><li>The reader receives a usable checklist, decision rule or Korean phrase.</li><li>Material changes update the checked date.</li></ul>
  <h2>Time-sensitive information</h2><p>Guides show the date when their core information was last checked. Prices, schedules, entry rules and provider conditions can change without notice. Confirm a critical decision with the official source for your date and circumstances.</p>
  <h2>Corrections</h2><p>If a source has changed or a guide is unclear, use our <a href="/contact/">public corrections channel</a>. Include the page URL, the statement in question and an official source when possible.</p>
  <h2>Commercial independence</h2><p>Advertising and future affiliate relationships may fund the site. They do not purchase favorable editorial conclusions. Affiliate links will be disclosed on the page where they appear.</p>
  <h2>What we are not</h2><p>Dama Korea is not a government agency, law firm, financial adviser, immigration representative or medical provider. Our guides provide general educational information and cannot replace advice for an individual case.</p>
</article></BaseLayout>
